[15:05:03] WARNING  [A Hardy Mystery] Solver blocked: A Hardy Mystery (ch36) is an on-site physical challenge. Live description recovered from the authenticated CTFd challenge modal: 'Someone from the future went into the past, and made a mess of the conference! / Instead of sane challenges that we could just one-shot, they... left us a message. / I think... I think we're going to have to touch grass this conference. / Start with the message. They were apparently a really big fan of those books at the front of the room.' WARNING: books must stay on the table (only radios may be removed); players may thumb through the books. Flag-format note: 'The flag technically is not in standard format. Because ... the left Brace { and right Brace } characters don't exist in the books! I had to improvise.' So the flag has NO braces and is built from the text/titles of the Hardy Boys books plus an on-site printed 'message' on the table. Author @solarbonite; series sponsored by The Coding Hackers. Key correction for siblings: the badge barcode flag sun{ctf_r_4_h00m4n5} is NOT this challenge (submitted -> Incorrect); it belongs to 'This Code's Got Bars!' (barcode layer in badge-gallery/bsidesorlando-2026 hardware/uv_art.psd). Also tested and rejected on ch36: The Tower Treasure, The Hardy Boys, sunhardyboys, sunthehardyboys, 'the butler did it', The Secret of the Old Mill, The House on the Cliff. Other BSides Orlando chals observed live: Layers of Secrets (3), Serious Business (19), Lil Chompy and the World's Fair (6), Drop dead, like an alligator. (6), Ishq FM 104.8? (4), Get rotated, man! (2).
